WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Three men at the top: a
general in a fortress,

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.180
an old king on a heath, a
prince on night battlements.

3
00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:11.990
The prince sees trouble coming:
"The time is out of joint.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.120
O cursed spite," The
old king, in the storm,

5
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.890
calls himself "More sinn’d
against than sinning."

6
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:24.320
A crack runs across each
man, then across each world.

7
00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:28.240
So where is the flaw: in
the hero, or the world?

8
00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:31.860
In this mission, you'll find the
pattern these three plays share,

9
00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.330
from the opening scenes to the fall.

10
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.760
You'll look closely at Hamlet's couplet.

11
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.680
And you'll hear critics
argue it both ways.

12
00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:42.830
Your mission: decide where the flaw lies,

13
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.750
in the hero or the world.
